00:02:20,706 --> 00:03:15,239
This is step 7, page 7. The right triangles divided by the bisector of the two internal angles become RHA congruent with the common hypotenuse + right angle + acute angle congruent, so that the distances to all three sides become the same, and the two right triangles at the last vertex become RHS congruent, completing the principle of bisecting the third angle. What you must remember at this time is that the circumcenter is the same distance to the 'three vertices' (OA=OB=OC), and the incenter is the same distance to the 'foot of the perpendicular line on the three sides' (ID=IE=IF=r). It is also directly connected to the formula for the area of ​​the triangle: S = 1/2·r·(a+b+c).

